You don't need a browser to verify a token. You can query the Solana RPC directly using `getAccountInfo` or `getTokenSupply`. In TypeScript with `@solana/web3.js`:

```typescript
import { getMint } from '@solana/spl-token';

const mintInfo = await getMint(connection, mintPublicKey);
const isMintRevoked = mintInfo.mintAuthority === null;
const isFreezeRevoked = mintInfo.freezeAuthority === null;
console.log({ isMintRevoked, isFreezeRevoked });
```
If both values are `null`, the supply is hard-capped and no holder accounts can be frozen.
